+
+/*
+ * Where the last scanned-out frame lives in guest memory.
+ *
+ * With no GL display path the Vulkan renderer downloads the frame into
+ * guest VRAM and has nothing to present it with, which is correct: the host
+ * presents now. This hands the host a CPU pointer to those pixels so it can
+ * do what it likes with them, which today is a PNG and on visionOS is a
+ * Metal texture upload.
